{"id": "obs:loka-lajja", "name": "Shame before people and family honour (lok-lāj)", "category": "bond", "description": "Concern for public opinion and family honour that keeps one from wholehearted devotion; Mīrā casts it off, and Tulsī counsels giving up even dear ones who do not love Rāma.", "lineages": ["lin:mirabai", "lin:ramanandi"], "names": [{"lineage": "lin:mirabai", "name": "lok-lāj, kul-kī-maryādā", "term": "trm:loka-lajja"}], "sources": [{"source": "src:mira-padavali", "ref": "mere-to-giridhara", "rests_on": ["tea:mira-padavali:mere-to-giridhara"]}, {"source": "src:bhaktamal", "ref": "mira", "rests_on": ["tea:bhaktamal:mira"]}, {"source": "src:vinaya-patrika", "ref": "174", "rests_on": ["tea:vinaya-patrika:174"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:satsanga", "total refuge in Giridhar"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:jati-abhimana", "name": "Pride of caste", "category": "passion", "description": "Pride in birth, which the saints say kills devotion (Tukārām: 'well that you made me a Kuṇbī, or I would have died of pride') and which excludes the low-born from God's house.", "lineages": ["lin:varkari", "lin:ramanandi", "lin:radhavallabha", "lin:ekasarana"], "sources": [{"source": "src:tukaram-gatha", "ref": "bare-deva-kunbi", "rests_on": ["tea:tukaram-gatha:bare-deva-kunbi"]}, {"source": "src:kavitavali", "ref": "7.106", "rests_on": ["tea:kavitavali:7.106"]}, {"source": "src:vyas-vani", "ref": "true-devotee", "rests_on": ["tea:vyas-vani:true-devotee"]}], "antidotes": ["remembering that outward birth does not touch devotion (Cokhāmeḷā's sugarcane)"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:dambha", "name": "Hypocrisy (dambha)", "category": "passion", "description": "Outward religiosity — bathing, marks, rosaries, rites — without inner purity or knowledge of the Self.", "lineages": ["lin:varkari", "lin:regional-bhakti-poets", "lin:radhavallabha"], "sources": [{"source": "src:tukaram-gatha", "ref": "nahi-nirmala-jivana", "rests_on": ["tea:tukaram-gatha:nahi-nirmala-jivana"]}, {"source": "src:narsinh-mehta-padas", "ref": "jyam-lagi-atma", "rests_on": ["tea:narsinh-mehta-padas:jyam-lagi-atma"]}], "antidotes": ["inner purity", "knowledge of the Self", "the saints' company"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:manasa-roga", "name": "The diseases of the mind (Rāmcaritmānas)", "category": "affliction", "description": "Delusion (moha) is the root; lust is wind, greed phlegm, anger bile; jealousy, pride, hypocrisy and the rest follow; cured only when Rāma's grace brings the true guru as physician, faith, restraint and devotion.", "lineages": ["lin:ramanandi"], "names": [{"lineage": "lin:ramanandi", "name": "mānas rog", "term": "trm:manasa-roga"}], "members": ["moha", "kāma", "lobha", "krodha", "mamatā", "īrṣyā", "mada", "dambha"], "sources": [{"source": "src:ramcaritmanas", "ref": "7.121-122", "rests_on": ["tea:ramcaritmanas:7.121-122"]}], "antidotes": ["the true guru's word", "faith", "restraint", "prc:navadha-bhakti"], "equivalents": [{"target": "obs:ari-sadvarga", "grade": "partial", "standpoint": "", "note": "overlapping list of passions, here cast as bodily humours with delusion at the root", "rests_on": ["tea:ramcaritmanas:7.121-122"]}], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:siddhi-abhimana", "name": "Pride in powers", "category": "obstacle", "description": "Powers (siddhi) and the pride they breed: Cāṅgadev's power over beasts was humbled; māyā sends the powers to blow out the lamp of knowledge; a guru who displays powers is false.", "lineages": ["lin:varkari", "lin:ramanandi", "lin:ramdasi"], "sources": [{"source": "src:bhaktavijaya", "ref": "flying-wall", "rests_on": ["tea:bhaktavijaya:flying-wall"]}, {"source": "src:ramcaritmanas", "ref": "7.115-120", "rests_on": ["tea:ramcaritmanas:7.115-120"]}, {"source": "src:dasbodh", "ref": "5.2", "rests_on": ["tea:dasbodh:5.2"]}], "antidotes": ["devotion (the self-luminous gem)", "the true guru"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:paraninda", "name": "Speaking ill of others", "category": "other", "description": "Slander and fault-finding, which the true Vaiṣṇava avoids and the saint does not see even in dreams.", "lineages": ["lin:regional-bhakti-poets", "lin:ramanandi"], "sources": [{"source": "src:narsinh-mehta-padas", "ref": "vaisnava-jana", "rests_on": ["tea:narsinh-mehta-padas:vaisnava-jana"]}, {"source": "src:ramcaritmanas", "ref": "3.35-36", "rests_on": ["tea:ramcaritmanas:3.35-36"]}], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:maya-i-and-mine", "name": "'I and mine' as māyā", "category": "bond", "description": "The sense of 'I' and 'mine', 'you' and 'yours' is the māyā that holds all beings (Rāma to Lakṣmaṇa).", "lineages": ["lin:ramanandi"], "sources": [{"source": "src:ramcaritmanas", "ref": "3.15", "rests_on": ["tea:ramcaritmanas:3.15"]}], "antidotes": ["devotion to Rāma"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:abhimana", "name": "Pride (abhimāna)", "category": "passion", "description": "Pride and the sense of self-importance: the root of sin (as popularly quoted from Tulsī), the fool's mark (Dāsbodh), what the true Vaiṣṇava never lets in (Narsinh), what made the Lord vanish from the gopīs (Keli-gopāla).", "lineages": ["lin:ramanandi", "lin:ramdasi", "lin:regional-bhakti-poets", "lin:ekasarana"], "sources": [{"source": "src:dasbodh", "ref": "2.1", "rests_on": ["tea:dasbodh:2.1"]}, {"source": "src:narsinh-mehta-padas", "ref": "vaisnava-jana", "rests_on": ["tea:narsinh-mehta-padas:vaisnava-jana"]}, {"source": "src:keli-gopala", "ref": "whole", "rests_on": ["tea:keli-gopala:whole"]}], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:ari-sadvarga", "name": "The six enemies (ariṣaḍvarga)", "category": "passion", "description": "Vārkarī and Rāmānandī usage: lust, anger, greed, delusion, pride and envy — the scorpion's venom of Eknāth's bhāruḍ; the Lord dwells only where they are absent.", "lineages": ["lin:varkari", "lin:ramanandi"], "sources": [{"source": "src:eknath-bharuds", "ref": "vincu-cavala", "rests_on": ["tea:eknath-bharuds:vincu-cavala"]}, {"source": "src:ramcaritmanas", "ref": "2.128-131", "rests_on": ["tea:ramcaritmanas:2.128-131"]}], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
